      "message": "Do you want `#[inline(always)]`? `#[inline]` is just a hint to the compiler. If this is load bearing in some cases (since you typed `fix`), you want `#[inline(always)]`. (Even that doesn\u0027t *force* it to be inline, for example if someone creates a function pointer out of it, but the optimizer will stop trying to make calls and just assume that if it can inline it should)",
